    "pipelineId": "item:ossuary:s14:outstanding_intake_tag",
    "name": "Outstanding Intake Tag",
    "type": "loot",
    "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/token-runed-os-grey.webp",
    "system": {
      "description": {
        "value": "<p>An old intake tag stamped with a crown mark. The number is very low.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-d6449c1b4d6c64b2\"><p><strong>GM note.</strong> T5, the third record. The party's sheets hold no Session 12 intake tags (checked in the live world when this item was built), so by the guide it is still in the passage under the Cladis memorial: History DC 12 to read the old numbering (Investigation DC 12 to pick it out if they took the tags after all). Second path: Rite of the Remaining Bone (Expose Claim, 10 minutes, a copper coin, no charges) shows the claim it belongs to. A party member with custody presents it to Pringus for a Reconciliation Audit. The audit is public: Tallis reads audits.</p></section>",
        "chat": ""
      },
      "source": {
